    "review": "What unfolds at Onondaga County War Memorial is a patchwork of highs and lows that keeps listeners guessing. The first set delivers a bright Let It Grow that showcases Garcia’s committed guitar work, yet Feel Like A Stranger closes on a weaker note, hinting at a band that never quite settles into full‑steam mode. The second set shines when the group locks into the classic Playing In The Band → Uncle John's Band transition, and Eyes Of The World adds a burst of melodic momentum, but elsewhere the performance feels sloppy – especially during extended jams where Garcia’s leads can sound “all over the place.”  The rhythm section stays solid, with Brent’s keyboards providing texture even when the overall energy dips. For fans who want to hear the show in its best possible fidelity, the 24‑bit FLAC recording captures the nuances without the bass‑heavy muddiness of some audience tapes.",
